WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.710
How would I teach civil engineering students in their first years?

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.700
I would start with one decision.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.370
A concrete building from the nineteen seventies.

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:17.100
Four options. Repair the minimum, renovate deeply, convert it to a new use, or demolish and build new.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.640
Students examine each option through four lenses:

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:28.590
technical condition, business cost over the life cycle, environmental impact, and the effect on the people who use the building.

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:37.560
Then they change seats. The owner, the user, the city and the contractor weigh those lenses differently, and the best option changes with them.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:39.890
There is no single right answer.

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:45.570
There is a well-argued one. That is system-level thinking, and it is what the profession will need.

